WEBVTT

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.500
<i>Alarm</i>

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.500
<i>Snooze</i>

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.500
<i>Stop</i>

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.800
<i>"Tanaka... you doing good?"</i>

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.290
<i>"I'm doing good in Shonan."</i>

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.060
The surf's rising!

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:43.020
Seems like today's the day I'll be able 
to have fun riding some waves!

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:06.920
Let's Go Surfing!!

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:25.200
Wave 6   Shonan Magic!

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:27.810
Morning, SG Hammer!

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.620
Good morning, Masaki.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.880
Morning, Tadao-san!

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:38.370
<i>"I was told that Tadao-san, the owner 
of the house, is a legendary shaper,"</i>

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.790
<i>"so I was nervous at first, but..."</i>

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:42.160
Masaki!

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:46.600
Banana juice? Or maybe apple juice?

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:47.790
Mixed!

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:49.890
Good choice!

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:54.070
<i>"...he's a really good person, 
so now we're getting along great!"</i>

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.400
I'm off!

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:19.090
Hammer! You need to walk on your own!

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.550
Come on, Hammer!

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:22.140
Good morning!

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:23.590
Morning!

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.630
Morning, Kosuke-san!

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:27.700
You're late.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.950
Huh? I woke up at five 
like I was supposed to!

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.810
If we're supposed to meet 
on the beach at five,

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.550
then you won't make it 
if you wake up at five.

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:34.390
That's true!

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:36.610
Now, now, Kosuke-san...

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:38.840
<i>"I'm getting along fine 
with Yuta and Kosuke-san,"</i>

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:38.840
He isn't that late.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.820
Don't coddle him, Yuta

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:42.800
<i>"so I wish I could say 
'everything's going great!' but..."</i>

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.800
This one instance is indicative 
of his general behavior!

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:48.480
There were waves until just a second ago!

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:50.710
That's Shonan magic for you.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:52.540
Shonan magic?

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.150
The waves disappear like magic.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:56.130
What?

00:03:56.130 --> 00:04:00.130
Who needs magic like that?

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:13.380
<i>There's no power in the waves, 
so I can't get any speed.</i>

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:23.320
Shonan only seems to have 
small waves day after day...

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:24.760
That isn't true.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.520
The kind of big waves you like 
come when they come!

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.840
Is that really true?

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:31.160
It's no lie.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:33.500
In Inamuragasaki,

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.320
there's a competition they only host 
when the waves are 3 meters or higher

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:40.670
called the Inamura Surfing Classic.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:46.590
After it was first held 
in the first year of Heisei, 1989,

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:51.540
they waited on the waves for 24 years 
and held it again in 2013.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.680
T-Twenty-four years?

00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:56.190
I'd love to be invited one day.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:57.440
It's something to dream about, right?

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:58.940
Don't give me "one day"!

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:02.690
I want to ride big waves now!

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:06.200
Hachirigahama Prefectural High School

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.710
How to attack small waves!

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:18.710
Let's think about how to attack these 
formulas instead of waves, all right?

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:22.020
Y-Yes, sir! I'm sorry.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.620
I want everyone to focus, all right?

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:30.280
Oh, man! I've gotta get it together.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:38.730
<i>How can I possibly study 
in a place like this?</i>

00:05:39.140 --> 00:05:41.760
<i>I'm sure he's thinking something like that.</i>

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:47.110
Good boy, Hammer.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:48.990
This time we won't be late-

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:52.790
Oh, how cute!

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.180
Oh! He answered me!

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.460
He's amazing!

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.450
You think he understands human language?

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:01.000
You seem to be in a very 
good mood, SG Hammer.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.910
He's called SG Hammer?

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.760
What a weird name.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.670
It's from "Shichiri Ga Hama." SG Hammer.

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:08.790
What?

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:10.120
That's hilarious!

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:17.590
Uh-oh!

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.470
Keeping people waiting because 
you were picking up girls...

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:22.790
You must feel pretty special.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:24.440
P-Picking up girls?

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:28.280
I-It wasn't like that! Hammer just 
went toward the girls, that's all...

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.230
Listen up.

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:34.270
Do not do anything that
 will tarnish surfers' images.

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:35.760
Images?

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:38.880
With the word "surfer," a lot
 of people have preconceptions

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:42.970
that we're just goofing off 
or playing around.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:46.410
For us, specifically, even though 
we don't belong to an official team,

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:48.860
we'll take time off of school to go compete.

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:53.550
For that reason, you 
can't neglect your studies.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:55.690
R-Right.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.130
Are you all right, Masaki?

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:01.980
I'm totally fine!

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.860
After all, he was on the mark 
about my schoolwork.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:08.520
I was the one who decided 
to go to this high school.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:10.280
I've gotta make sure to do it right.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:15.720
Masaki, you're a little bit like Kosuke-san.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:17.620
Huh? How?

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:20.980
Your passion, maybe?

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:24.880
Kosuke-san used to be 
a serious baseball player.

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.430
Really?

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:32.470
He was the ace in Little League,

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:34.930
and people were expecting 
great things from his future.

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:39.870
But he badly injured his elbow and had 
no choice but to give up baseball.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.060
What?

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:44.080
That's when he started surfing.

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:53.830
Around here, there are a lot of surfers

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:57.660
who have been surfing since they were born.

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:02.470
To try to catch up, 
he often practiced too hard...

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:03.640
I see...

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:05.630
Kosuke-san is really amazing.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.210
The waves are going to disappear 
while you're chatting.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:12.320
Huh?

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:13.800
Wha— Kosuke-san?

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.620
He holds a weight 
and runs along the seafloor.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:20.570
It's practice, so that he can withstand 
getting wiped out by any wave.

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:21.710
Really?

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:23.300
Okay! I'm going, too!

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:46.010
Loco moco for Masaki and Kosuke, right?

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:48.590
And for Yuta, his usual shirasu-don!

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:50.340
Here.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.460
Thank you very much.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:55.660
Sorry for always making you
 cook enough for us, too.

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:57.290
Don't worry!

00:08:57.290 --> 00:09:00.930
It's fun watching young people eat a lot.

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.300
Yuta...

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:05.600
I feel like you're eventually going to 
eat up all the shirasu in the ocean.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:07.830
Me?

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.440
Well, let's see...

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:13.330
First, if we think about it 
in terms of just Kanagawa,

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:17.110
the shirasu catch in the span 
of a year is 400 to 600 tons.

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:22.390
One shirasu-don uses, 
on average, 732 shirasu, so...

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:23.330
for me to eat all the—

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:24.620
Enough already. Just eat!

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:26.980
Thank you for the meal!

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:35.070
Tadao-san! This hamburger is super yummy!

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:38.390
Yeah! There's cream puffs for later.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:39.640
Yay!

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:42.620
Oh! Tadao-san, can I have 
some more barley tea?

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:46.240
Okay! Wait just a minute.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:48.500
Hey, Masaki!

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:49.170
Huh?

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:51.150
Get the barley tea yourself!

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:54.650
You know how incredible a board 
shaper Tadao-san is, don't you?

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:56.070
Of course I do!

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:58.880
But Tadao-san is so nice, I just end up...

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.710
I can understand how you feel.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:06.450
Tadao-san always interacts 
with us frankly, after all.

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:08.420
That's true, but...

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:11.670
You're helping with the housework, right?

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:12.940
I am!

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:16.550
I take Hammer for walks, 
and... clean up and...

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:21.300
After we eat the cream puffs, 
we're cleaning.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.530
Okay!

00:10:42.340 --> 00:10:44.350
Hey. What's up?

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:48.040
Tadao-san... Shape a board for me!

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:49.080
Okay.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:50.830
What? Really?

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:53.090
Well, it is my job.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:56.760
Whether it's for a beginner or a pro...

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:59.990
I'll make the best board for that person.

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:04.450
I can't seem to ride 
the waves in Shonan very well.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:06.420
With one of your boards, Tadao-san, 
I might be able to do it!

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:07.840
But it'll cost you.

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:10.600
Very, very expensive.

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:16.110
Recent off-the-shelf boards 
are impressively high-performance.

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:18.940
They're more than enough 
for you right now, Masaki.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:20.210
But...

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:22.510
Style is everything.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:23.370
Huh?

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.490
Masaki, you don't see it yet, do you?

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:36.370
To think he can ask Tadao-san so simply...

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:38.510
He's an impressive guy, that Masaki.

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:42.870
<i>You really don't get it at all.</i>

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:03.160
<i>Yeah. They do say that 
the waves in Shonan are small.</i>

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:05.200
Yeah, they are.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:07.420
What are the waves like in Hawaii?

00:12:07.420 --> 00:12:09.910
Like I even have to ask...

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:13.590
<i>Hawaiian waves are awesome!</i>

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:17.190
<i>Huzzah, long live pipeline!</i>

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:22.600
Aw, man. I want to ride 
some big waves in Hawaii, too.

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:28.090
<i>But the ocean in Shonan 
is closest to the world stage.</i>

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:30.960
<i>There are top-class surfers 
and sponsors there.</i>

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:32.130
<i>And, most importantly...</i>

00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:34.440
<i>Tadao-san is there.</i>

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:36.460
Well... that's true.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:39.360
<i>"Waves are toys from God."</i>

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:43.200
<i>No matter what kind of waves they are, 
go have some fun, Corgi.</i>

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:45.460
I will!

00:12:45.460 --> 00:12:48.360
<i>Well, I'm going to sleep soon, so...</i>

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:50.450
<i>I'm waiting for you in Hawaii!</i>

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:53.350
<i>Aloha!</i>

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.300
Yeah! Let's go again tomorrow!

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.300
Good work today.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:02.340
Yeah! Let's go again tomorrow!

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:02.340
Good work today.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:04.820
<i>"Did you watch episode 9 of </i>Magical Miruru<i>?"</i>

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:07.350
<i>"Yeah, I watched it!"</i>

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:10.300
<i>"I never imagined Miruru and 
MaiMai would end up like that..."</i>

00:13:13.670 --> 00:13:15.890
<i>"Miruru-san's so cool!"</i>

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:17.860
<i>"The Miruru rabbit-hole is deep, for real..."</i>

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:25.740
Kido Naoya
 Miruru △
 The Miruru rabbit-hole is deep, for real...

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:28.730
<i>"SG Hammer-chan is so cute!"</i>

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:33.160
<i>"Isokichi is so lonely 
without you here, Big Brother."</i>

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.380
<i>"You're not homesick, are you?"</i>

00:13:43.350 --> 00:13:46.910
"I'm not sick with missing home. 
I'm missing Oarai's waves!"

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:51.890
Oh, right! I have to ask 
for dried sweet potatoes.

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:56.390
"I run out of dried sweet potatoes really 
fast, so please send a whole box."

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:09.880
Have fun no matter what 
the waves are like...

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:12.090
Okay!

00:14:12.090 --> 00:14:16.040
Tomorrow, I'm getting to the beach 
before Kosuke-san and Yuta!

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.830
Alarm

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.340
I'm begging you, Hammer!

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:24.380
Today I want to be the first one out there!

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:27.430
Morning!

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:30.930
I really thought I'd be 
earlier than you today.

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:33.720
Um, Kosuke-san...

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:34.950
Masaki.

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:38.440
At this rate, I will never 
be able to respect you.

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:39.270
Huh?

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:40.840
You're late again and again.

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:42.210
He's improved.

00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:43.720
You flirt with girls.

00:14:43.720 --> 00:14:45.440
That was a misunderstanding...

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:46.770
You don't study, either!

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:48.950
He said he'd do better.

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:50.320
And, more than anything else...

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:54.200
that disrespectful attitude toward 
Shonan's sea and Tadao-san!

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.700
What?

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:58.810
You said you were aiming 
for the world stage, right?

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:02.600
Whether you are a man worthy 
of such big talk or not...

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:04.630
I will decide that here and now!

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:09.220
I challenge you, Masaki!

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:11.530
Ch-Challenge?

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:29.990
<i>I guess... I must have made him angry 
about lots of things without realizing it.</i>

00:15:30.980 --> 00:15:34.720
<i>In that case, I'll make Kosuke-san 
understand me through my surfing!</i>

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:36.370
<i>I'll show him that I'm serious!</i>

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:40.870
<i>I mean, I spent all that time 
riding waves in Oarai!</i>

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:47.500
All right!

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:52.880
He's going with that wave?

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:56.890
He's fast!

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:05.020
I wonder if this will help 
Masaki understand.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:07.350
No two waves are alike.

00:16:07.350 --> 00:16:10.720
It's all about how you use 
each individual wave's power.

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:14.530
Successfully riding difficult waves that
 ask a lot in terms of technical prowess

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:17.100
can also be looked 
at as riding aggressively!

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:19.550
I get it!

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:22.790
No matter what the waves are like, 
having fun is up to me!

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:27.670
<i>More, more...</i>

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.940
<i>Faster than Kosuke-san!</i>

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:42.310
Whoa! Amazing!

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:50.320
Kosuke-san's forgotten that
they're supposed to be competing.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:58.700
He's the type that always gets fired up 
when he sees amazing surfers.

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:00.080
Yuta!

00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:02.580
Let's go surfing!

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:05.010
Coming!

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:35.490
Kosuke... san...

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:41.390
My name... how...

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:44.730
My mom told me there's 
someone in the neighborhood

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.710
who is amazing at baseball.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:51.500
I can't play baseball anymore...

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:56.840
I messed up my elbow, so...

00:17:57.900 --> 00:17:59.990
They said I can't.

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:03.120
But I just couldn't believe it, so...

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:05.640
Today, I went to practice, and...

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:09.800
Everyone looked at me 
like they pitied me...

00:18:10.220 --> 00:18:13.820
That's when... I knew it was real...

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:20.960
Kosuke-san.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:25.410
Want to try surfing?

00:18:26.360 --> 00:18:31.420
Playing around... in the ocean? 
I'm not in the mood.

00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:34.280
It's not playing.

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:35.340
Huh?

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:37.550
You'll understand if you try it.

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:19.800
Man, that felt good!

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:22.290
That's what I wanted to hear.

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:25.780
Kosuke-san! Is that why you challenged me?

00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:26.810
Huh?

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:28.200
Y-Yeah.

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:29.820
No, it wasn't, was it?

00:19:29.820 --> 00:19:32.060
At the beginning, 
you were just angry, right?

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:35.280
Honestly.

00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:41.820
Somehow, I feel like I finally 
made friends with Shonan's ocean.

00:19:43.960 --> 00:19:46.560
To get along even better,

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:49.830
you should probably 
take off a little faster.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:52.070
And your board's angle 
of incidence to the wave...

00:19:52.070 --> 00:19:55.010
Wow! You're taking down my data, too?

00:19:55.010 --> 00:19:57.270
So what is it I need to focus on?

00:19:57.270 --> 00:19:58.840
Let me see the video!

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:00.450
There's no need to rush.

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:02.120
I'll explain everything in order.

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:03.870
Okay! I'm counting on you.

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:04.840
So, what's next?

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:15.740
Shonan's ocean showed me 
where I'm lacking right now.

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:18.930
It told me to get better and better!

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:22.610
Yes. That's Shonan's ocean.

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:24.820
It's the best ocean in Japan.

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:28.760
No. The best in Japan is Oarai!

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:31.870
It's true that Shonan is good too, 
but I'm not budging on this!

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:33.070
It's Shonan!

00:20:33.070 --> 00:20:34.120
Oarai!

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.210
Shonan!

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:35.960
Oarai!

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:40.600
A surfer's love for his hometown 
can be quite problematic.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:36.870
Shonan!

00:20:36.870 --> 00:20:38.150
Oarai!

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:40.600
What do you think, Yuta? It's Oarai, right?

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:41.780
It's Shonan!

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:47.570
<i>"Today, we got some nice waves in Hawaii!"</i>

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:49.440
<i>"Did you have fun, too?"</i>

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:55.560
<i>"In a single moment, I completely 
fell in love with Shonan's ocean."</i>

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.660
<i>"Is this Shonan magic, too?"</i>

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:04.220
Wow...

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:13.120
Do you want beef for dinner today? 
Or do you want chicken?

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:15.670
Both!

00:21:17.370 --> 00:21:19.170
So young!

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:22.500
What were you looking at?

00:21:22.500 --> 00:21:25.500
The night view. I was thinking 
about how pretty it is.

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:29.390
Beautiful!

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:31.680
Those are the lights from Hayama.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:34.020
Really? Hayama...

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:34.860
Huh?

00:21:37.110 --> 00:21:40.100
No... It's nothing.

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:47.500
Okay! Today it's a chicken 
and beef double steak plate.

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:49.370
I'll call you when it's ready.

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:51.350
Thank you, Tadao-san!

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:58.810
<i>Hayama...</i>

00:21:58.810 --> 00:22:00.880
<i>the town where Sho used to live.</i>

00:22:01.390 --> 00:22:04.960
<i>It made me feel like Sho 
was watching over me somehow.</i>

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:08.880
<i>There, in the lights of Hayama, I swore...</i>

00:22:09.810 --> 00:22:12.810
<i>Sho, I'm going to do my best here!</i>

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:17.640
<i>Aiming higher... Aiming for the world!</i>

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:53.990
Wave 7
A Heart Adrift Between the Waves
